    answer: "On the 6.0L Power Stroke, engine oil travels from the pan and pickup to the front-cover gerotor pump, through pressure regulation, then through the valley-mounted oil cooler and top-mounted filter. Filtered oil supplies the HPOP reservoir, turbocharger, left and right tappet galleries, piston-cooling jets, cam bearings, main bearings, and rod bearings before draining back to the pan.",
    detail: "The oil cooler is a liquid-to-liquid heat exchanger: engine oil and coolant pass through separate internal passages. A coolant-side restriction can reduce cooler and EGR-cooler performance without representing the same fault as low base-engine oil pressure.",
