    answer: "A Gen I Chevy 350 normally seals its main oil drillings with plugs at the rear of the block and at the front behind the timing set, but plug style, depth, quantity and access vary by block casting and machining. Identify the casting, remove the cam bearings when required for cleaning, trace every drilled passage, and follow the exact block or crate-engine instructions before installation.",
    detail: "This page distinguishes oil-galley plugs from coolant core plugs, block drains, threaded sender ports and oil-filter adapter/bypass parts. Confusing those features can cause immediate loss of oil pressure or internal leakage.",
