    answer: "There is no single Ford 4.6 V8 timing-mark diagram. A 2-valve SOHC 4.6 uses two primary chains, one from the crankshaft to each camshaft. A 3-valve SOHC engine also has bank-specific primary chains but adds variable-cam-timing phasers and a different holding/alignment procedure. A 4-valve DOHC engine uses two primary chains plus two secondary chains to time four camshafts. Identify the engine by VIN, model year, cylinder-head/cam-cover architecture and service-manual application before placing any colored link or releasing a tensioner.",
