    answer: "The Ford 5.4L 3V uses two primary timing chains, one for each cylinder bank, and a variable-cam-timing phaser on each camshaft. Alignment requires the exact workshop-manual crank position, the designated colored chain links placed at the crank-sprocket and phaser timing marks, correct left/right guides and tensioners, and phasers fully seated on their camshaft alignment pins. Ford warns that incorrect phaser alignment or retaining-bolt torque can deform or shear the pin and cause rattle, rough running or a check-engine light.",
