      "Set No. 1 cylinder to TDC/compression. With covers installed, align the crank pulley groove to 0 and confirm both cam references align; rotate the crank 360 degrees if cams are on the opposite stroke.",
      "With the belt exposed, align the crankshaft timing-pulley mark to the oil-pump-body mark.",
      "Align the RH camshaft knock-pin hole to the RH timing mark on the No. 3 cover. Align the LH cam-pulley timing mark to the LH cover mark.",
      "Inspect belt teeth/backing, idlers, tensioner, water pump, seals and pulley flanges. Correct every oil/coolant leak before installing a clean belt.",
      "Install the belt in the order prescribed by the Toyota procedure, matching printed installation lines where supplied and maintaining tension between the crank and cam pulleys on the designated non-tensioned spans.",
