    answer: "At No. 1 cylinder TDC on a Honda B16A, align the timing mark on the crankshaft timing-belt drive pulley with the pointer on the oil-pump housing. Position both cam pulleys with their UP marks at the top. The horizontal TDC index lines on the intake and exhaust cam pulleys must align with the cylinder-head upper surface and with each other. Keep the crank and cams at those fixed references while installing and tensioning the belt, then rotate the crank counterclockwise by hand and recheck all marks.",
