      "Inspect cam/crank pulley teeth, keys, belt, tensioner, water pump and seals. Correct oil or coolant leakage and keep the new belt clean and dry.",
      "Route the belt in the sequence specified by the Honda manual, keeping tension on the non-tensioner spans so neither cam moves a tooth.",
      "Apply belt tension with the manual's crank-rotation and tensioner-bolt sequence. Do not pry against the belt or substitute a generic deflection value.",
