    title: "Nissan VQ35DE Timing Chain Alignment: Primary and Secondary Marks",
    metaDescription: "Nissan VQ35DE timing-chain alignment guide explaining the primary chain, two secondary chains, bank-specific cam marks, colored links, tensioners and verification.",
    answer: "The VQ35DE uses one primary chain from the crankshaft sprocket to both intake-cam sprockets and two secondary chains, one per bank, connecting each intake cam to its exhaust cam. Set No. 1 cylinder at TDC/compression using the exact vehicle manual. Match every marked chain link to its punched, notched or stamped sprocket reference, keeping right- and left-bank secondary marks separate. On the cited longitudinal FX35 procedure, circle-type marks identify the right bank and oval-type marks the left bank, and the intake references are read from the rear side. Link colors and mark shapes can differ in transverse applications, so do not copy a color-only diagram across vehicles.",
    detail: "Colored links are installation aids, not recurring inspection marks. After the crank is rotated, the links normally will not return to all sprocket marks after only two revolutions even though mechanical timing is correct. Final proof is smooth controlled hand rotation, correct fixed sprocket relationships at the manual's reference position, correct tensioner deployment and valid cam/crank correlation after startup.",
    scope: "Base VQ35DE applications after VIN, model year and longitudinal-versus-transverse layout verification. It does not automatically cover VQ35DE Rev Up, VQ35HR or VQ37VHR engines. Front/rear timing-case sealing, VVT sprocket handling, chain-link colors and torque/angle procedures must come from the exact Nissan or Infiniti service manual.",
