    detail: "Mitsubishi produced 12-valve SOHC, 24-valve SOHC and 24-valve DOHC 6G72 engines in transverse and longitudinal applications. Rear-cover pointers, tensioner style and component access vary among Diamante, 3000GT/Stealth, Eclipse/Galant, Montero/Pajero and Chrysler applications. Use the engine's actual head/sprocket count, VIN and vehicle manual—not the 6G72 casting alone.",
    scope: "Mitsubishi 6G72 3.0L gasoline engines after vehicle, year, head type, valve count and turbo status verification. The map is an identification and workflow guide; exact mark artwork, tensioner preload, pin clearance, bolt torque and belt part number must come from the matching factory publication.",
