    metaDescription: "Audi 2.7T APB/BEL timing-belt guide explaining TDC, crank pin 3242, cam bar 3391, inward cam-plate holes, floating sprockets, tensioning and verification.",
    answer: "For an Audi 2.7T APB timing-belt installation, turn the crank clockwise to cylinder-3 TDC as defined by the workshop procedure, align the crank pulley marks, and confirm the large holes in the two camshaft locking plates face inward toward each other. Engage crank locking pin 3242 through the left block plug hole and fit camshaft bar 3391 across the two plates. Loosen both taper-fit cam sprockets and pull them free so they can float, install and pretension the belt with the cams and crank locked, then tighten the cam sprockets. Paint marks alone cannot reproduce the correct tension distribution.",
    detail: "The 2.7T belt drives the exhaust camshaft on each bank; short chains and hydraulic adjusters drive the intake cams inside the cylinder heads. The APB factory procedure uses a slowly compressed oil-damped tensioning element, locking pin T40011 and a 15 N·m roller pretension before cam-sprocket tightening. BEL production and updated tensioner kits must be matched by VIN and parts data rather than assumed identical.",
    scope: "Audi 2.7L five-valve V6 biturbo engines after exact engine-code and VIN verification, principally North American APB and BEL. European AGB/AZB/ARE/BES applications, RS4 derivatives, updated tensioner hardware and any cam-chain service require their own erWin procedure and parts information.",
