    title: "Nissan KA24DE Head Bolt Torque Sequence and Five Stages",
    metaDescription: "Nissan KA24DE head-bolt guide: 29 N·m, 79 N·m, full release, 25–34 N·m and 86–91°, plus oiling, angle-mark and timing-chain checks.",
    answer: "For the cited Nissan KA24DE applications, apply new engine oil to the production head-bolt threads and seat surfaces. Tighten all head bolts in Nissan's numerical order to 29 N·m (22 lb-ft), then 79 N·m (59 lb-ft); loosen every bolt completely; tighten all again to 25–34 N·m (18–25 lb-ft); then repeat the order and turn each bolt 86–91 degrees clockwise. Use an angle wrench, or paint-mark each bolt on the side facing the engine front and measure the turn. This five-stage procedure is confirmed in the 1997 240SX and cited 2001–2004 Frontier/Xterra manuals, but the surrounding timing/front-cover workflow remains application-specific.",
